package/shairport-sync: bump to a pinned 5.6-dev snapshot

Pin development commit 94070a1d514229b03a1ca202297a20a8993d6d92 for
AirPlay 2 remote controls, the security fixes, restored sender volume
sliders with ignore_volume_control, and plist metadata on D-Bus.
Stable 5.5.2 does not contain the development branch's AP2 controls.
Use the full commit as the version and archive name, not a moving tag
or branch.

AirPlay 2 generates its /info response from an XML plist at build time.
Add host-libplist for plistutil alongside the existing host-vim for
xxd. Disable Cython bindings in the host package too. Buildroot's
libglib2 dependency already supplies host-libglib2 for gdbus-codegen.

Keep the audio pipe backend and native D-Bus/MPRIS interfaces. The
latter enable metadata, the metadata hub and remote controls without
--with-metadata, which also enables the unused legacy metadata FIFO.
Explicitly disable that FIFO; BoomPi reads metadata from D-Bus.

The D-Bus XML and service sources moved under dbus/, which upstream's
Makefile.am handles. Both policy files and shairport-sync.conf remain
under scripts/, so the recipe's installation paths stay unchanged.
AirPlay 2 implies FFmpeg including libswresample, already built by
Buildroot 2026.02 without a separate Kconfig option. NQPTP 1.2.4 still
provides smi10 for BoomPi's default single instance; the new optional
multi-instance support requires newer NQPTP. LICENSES and its hash are
unchanged. Buildroot 2026.02 has no shairport-sync patches to remove.

Applied to the Buildroot tree by CI (see buildroot-patches/ and
.github/workflows/image.yml). Companion changes rebase the BoomPi source
patches and pin the pipe format (AP2 defaults are 48 kHz/S32_LE rather
than 44.1 kHz/S16). RemoteControl remains available; Client is an additional
interface for raw plist metadata, not a replacement for RemoteControl.

